_insider_own":0.00301,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Darden Restaurants, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, owns and operates full-service restaurants in the United States and Canada. The company operates under Olive Garden, LongHorn Steakhouse, Cheddar's Scratch Kitchen, Chuy's, Yard House, Ruth's Chris Steak House, The Capital Grille, Seasons 52, Eddie V's Prime Seafood, Bahama Breeze, The Capital Burger, Darden and Darden Restaurants brand names. Darden Restaurants, Inc. was founded in 1938 and is based in Orlando, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ricardo  Cardenas CPA | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $6.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 209K people. Revenue per employee of $63K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $5K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $377 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 104\u00d7 revenue per employee (high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Darden Restaurants, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $27.5B market cap on $13.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 37% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 29-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 19% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.54\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 30% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.30115080543971995},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.6M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2611763.25},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Darden Restaurants (NYSE:DRI) Finally Turning The Corner?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/is-darden-restaurants-nysedri-finally-turning-the-corner","date":"2026-11-22","timestamp":1795336440.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Darden (DRI) Stock Looks Fully Valued On Its 8% Dividend Raise","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/darden-dri-stock-looks-fully-191042529.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795201842.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.949,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Darden Restaurants (DRI) Sets December Earnings Date As Fair Value Debate Tightens","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/darden-restaurants-dri-sets-december-181411006.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795198451.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.932,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"US Jobs Report Could Shift DICK'S Sporting Goods Stock And Other Consumer Winners","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/us-jobs-report-could-shift-211548061.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795814148.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.802,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Invest in Big Macs, Whoppers and Olive Garden Breadsticks for Passive Income: $90,000 Across These 3 Restaurant Stocks P