ion of 1.54x.","ROE of 55% is amplified by 5.8x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.6% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.7x net debt to EBITDA ($219.5M of cash against $1.6B of debt), with interest covered 12.5x.","The current ratio of 0.31 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 8.0% over 3 years, 12.9% over 5 years and 6.7% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 3.6% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 115%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.3x, 5.6% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 21, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 99%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (5 sales, net $2.6M sold).","It returns 4.9% a year to shareholders (2.3% in buybacks and 2.7% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 2.7% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 30 consecutive years, raising it 27.9% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 209,931 employees, each generates about $63K of revenue, 0.2x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 3.9% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $5K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $6.6M (104x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (8/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"score":53.0,"head":"Red flag: priced 30% above its fair value of $187.","pros":["Composite 53, above the 39 line (gates 15/26)","ROIC 37.0% vs WACC 7.9%","Revenue grew 12.9%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.7x","Piotroski F-score 7/9"],"cons":["Trades 30% above fair value of $18